From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ali Abdolahi <i@abdolahi.info>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 02:42:56 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] TelephonyProvider: request MANAGE_APP_OPS_MODES for itself

SmsProvider checks each stored message for a one-time code and, once the
check is done, updates the row. That update notifies the default SMS
application through ProviderUtil.notifyIfNotDefaultSmsApp, which looks
it up with SmsApplication.getApplication(updateIfNeeded=true). That call
gives the application its exclusive SMS app-ops when they are not
allowed (tryFixExclusiveSmsAppops) and then reasserts the system apps'
modes (defaultSmsAppChanged). Both use AppOpsManager.setUidMode, which
requires MANAGE_APP_OPS_MODES.

The provider runs in the android.uid.phone shared uid and has always
relied on TeleService, which shares that uid, to request the permission.
A product that ships TelephonyProvider for received messages but no
TeleService leaves the uid without it: every message carrying a code
then throws SecurityException on the provider's executor and kills the
com.android.phone process.

Request the permission in the provider's own manifest. It is a signature
permission and the provider is platform-signed, so it is granted; with
TeleService present the uid already holds it, so nothing changes there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 AndroidManifest.xml | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/AndroidManifest.xml b/AndroidManifest.xml
index 8744212e641c037840e170b2615bab15a59c6b5f..094cd2f98286b7bd033f013c8c7e923dc2a7d6c1 100644
--- a/AndroidManifest.xml
+++ b/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -53,6 +53,11 @@
     <!-- Needed to query for whether the device is managed by an enterprise admin -->
     <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.MANAGE_USERS"/>
     <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.QUERY_DOMAIN_VERIFICATION" />
+    <!-- Needed to give the default SMS application its exclusive app-ops
+         (SmsApplication.getApplication), which ProviderUtil reaches through the
+         OTP check. TeleService requests it for this shared uid; a product without
+         TeleService must request it here. -->
+    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.MANAGE_APP_OPS_MODES" />
 
     <application android:process="com.android.phone"
                  android:allowClearUserData="false"
